WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.447
Now we look in the opposite direction.

00:00:02.447 --> 00:00:10.657
The S Q L function spelled L E A D returns a value from a later row in the sequence.

00:00:10.657 --> 00:00:15.878
To make the spoken explanation clearer, think of it as the next-value function.

00:00:16.328 --> 00:00:24.265
If lag answers, what happened before this row, the next-value function answers, what happens after this row.

00:00:24.265 --> 00:00:32.314
This can be useful for time until the next visit, next purchase, next website event, or next status change.
